.\"	$NetBSD$
.\"
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt MOUNT_APFS 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mount_apfs
.Nd mount an Apple File System
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl o Ar options
.Ar special
.Ar node
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility attaches an Apple File System (APFS) on
.Ar special
to the file system tree at the point
.Ar node .
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width indent
.It Fl o
Options are specified with a
.Fl o
flag followed by a comma-separated string of options.
See the
.Xr mount 8
man page for possible options and their meanings.
.El
.Sh NOTES
The APFS implementation is read-only. It validates sealed-volume integrity
metadata and hashes for hashed file-system B-tree nodes, but does not yet
support encrypted objects or file-data hash verification. A volume whose
required metadata is encrypted cannot be mounted.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mount 2 ,
.Xr mount 8
.Sh HISTORY
The
.Nm
utility first appeared in
.Nx 11.0 .
.Sh AUTHORS
The
.Nx
implementation of APFS was written by Junie.
